# Female — THE WIDOW, authored from a description, no measurement step (the
# soldier's method: describe-and-judge, see commit "plan + refs: a female
# character, authored from a description"). The reference plate
# (docs/dev-notes/refs/female-example-views-ref.png) was read once for
# proportions — hourglass, slim limbs, hair UP in a bun — and put down. The
# mesh was used ONLY to bake the face decal (blob:face-bake), filtered to its
# six head meshes; its clothes and its 722-joint Rigify rig are ignored.
#
# WHO SHE IS. The cast is a bestiary — a scheming goblin, a flesh-zombie, a
# jester-clown, an ordinary grunt — and the one ordinary-human slot is taken.
# What the Weird West has that this cast doesn't is its GOTHIC: the mourning
# widow in black, pale and cinched, hair piled up, one red cameo at the
# throat. She is the saloon's widow — dressed for a funeral she may have
# arranged. That puts a woman beside the goblin and the soldier without
# either figure-study realism or a second monster.
#
# THE THREE BEATS that carry her silhouette (same budget as the goblin's
# ears+nose+lips, the soldier's flat-top+pauldrons+belt, the clown's
# hat+nose+shoes):
#   1. THE BUN — oversized dark updo, the reference's loudest feature. From
#      behind and the side it is half the head's mass.
#   2. THE WASP WAIST — the corseted cinch. Shoulders and hips both read
#      wider than a waist pulled in hard; the hourglass is the reference's
#      proportion note and the widow's menace at once.
#   3. THE BLACK BLOCKS — dress, stockings, gloves, shoes as ONE near-black
#      plum mass broken only by pale skin (face, upper arms) and the single
#      red choker. Colour blocking does the clothing; no kit, no fine detail.
#
# Everything else is a supporting mass, in the house idiom: few large smooth
# prims, heavy blends, clothing as paint on the sculpt (the mouse/schoolgirl
# route — it costs no prims), the face a baked decal, never painted prims.

model female
  height 1.68
  # humanoid | digitigrade. Checked, not decorative — see blob-checks.ts.
  stance humanoid

skeleton
  # Legs are half the standing height, as on the soldier — she is the same
  # ordinary-human scale, an inch shorter in heels-down terms. Root at 0.85
  # so the leg chain (0.42 + 0.415 below the pelvis tail at 0.95) lands the
  # ankle at 0.115, the schoolgirl's ankle — her shoe prims then port
  # unchanged.
  root pelvis at 0.85 len=0.10

  # Upright with a whisper of backward lean — the widow stands straight; the
  # zombie owns the stoop, the goblin the hunch.
  bone spine1 parent=pelvis dir=up pitch=-1 len=0.15
  bone chest  parent=spine1 dir=up pitch=-1 len=0.15
  bone spine2 parent=chest  dir=up pitch=0  len=0.06
  bone neck   parent=spine2 dir=up pitch=0  len=0.075
  # Carries the face block: cranium centre ~1.48, chin ~1.41, flesh crown
  # ~1.57; the bun tops at ~1.66. Head about 1/8 of 1.68, cast-normal.
  bone skull  parent=neck   dir=up pitch=2  len=0.21

  mirror
    # Shoulder socket at x 0.128, y 1.31. The goblin lesson: shoulder reach
    # is a function of chest width — the yoke here is half-width ~0.10, so a
    # 0.028/0.10 clavicle lands the socket just proud of the dress.
    bone clavicle parent=spine2  side=0.028 dir=side  len=0.100
    # Arms hang DOWN and slightly OUT (tilt 8/6 clears the skirt by ~5 cm —
    # the schoolgirl measured the <=6 deg fog line where arm and waist melt).
    bone upperarm parent=clavicle dir=down tilt=8 pitch=2  len=0.23
    bone forearm  parent=upperarm dir=down tilt=6 pitch=10 len=0.21
    bone hand     parent=forearm  dir=down pitch=8         len=0.09
    # Legs: dead straight with a whisper of outward slant, like the soldier.
    bone thigh    parent=pelvis dir=down tilt=2 side=0.058 len=0.42
    bone shin     parent=thigh  dir=down tilt=2            len=0.415
    # The foot bone only positions the shoe prims (the house pattern).
    bone foot     parent=shin   dir=fwd                    len=0.12
  end

body
  # ============================================================
  # TORSO — the black dress IS these masses, painted. Near-black plum
  # (171219), not pure black: pure black reads as a hole under the lab's
  # single key. The hourglass lives here: yoke ~0.10 half, waist pulled to
  # 0.070, hips back out to 0.098.
  # ============================================================
  # Hips: the dress over the pelvis; the skirt shell flares below this.
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.45 r=0.104 wide=1.00 tall=0.95 deep=0.82 blend=0.008 color=171219
  # Waist: bar up spine1 (y 1.00 -> 1.10), cinched to 0.066 at the top — the
  # wasp waist sits just under the bust, where the reference's does.
  bar  torso on spine1 from=0.35 to=1.00 r=0.088 r2=0.066 deep=0.76 blend=0.006 color=171219
  # Bust: swelling from the cinch (0.072 at y 1.13) out to 0.102 at the
  # shoulder line (y 1.24), deep 0.92 for the side-profile read.
  bar  torso on chest  from=0.20 to=0.92 r=0.072 r2=0.102 deep=0.92 blend=0.008 color=171219
  # Bust mounds, front — the side-view bust of the reference, as geometry.
  blob torso on chest  at=0.55 offset=(0.042,0,0.055) r=0.055 deep=1.00 blend=0.006 both color=171219
  # High mourning collar up spine2 to the neck.
  bar  torso on spine2 from=0.00 to=0.90 r=0.082 r2=0.048 deep=0.78 blend=0.006 color=171219

  # ============================================================
  # THE SKIRT — one flared shell cone, black, knee-length (cloth, not mass —
  # the schoolgirl's skirt pattern). Waistband 0.072 half at y 1.00 flaring
  # to 0.170 at the hem (y 0.50, just above the knee), deep 0.80. tall 0.30
  # stays inside the renderer's anisotropy family (the schoolgirl's GPU-hole
  # lesson: no thinner than ~3x on the caps).
  # ============================================================
  shell torso on spine1 at=0.333 r=0.072 r2=0.170 tip=(0,-0.500,0) wide=1.00 tall=0.30 deep=0.80 thick=0.006 clip=(0,-1,0) clipd=-0.500 rim=0.007 blend=0.006 color=171219

  # Neck: pale skin above the collar.
  bar head on neck from=0.05 to=0.95 r=0.027 deep=1.15 blend=0.004

  # THE CAMEO CHOKER — the single red accent (8a1016). A flat band proud of
  # the throat, wide and squashed so it reads as a choker, not a bead.
  blob head on neck at=0.50 offset=(0,0,0.024) r=0.013 wide=1.40 tall=0.45 deep=0.90 blend=0.003 color=8a1016

  # ============================================================
  # HAIR — dark brown (261b12, the bake's hair) worn UP. Crown dome + fringe
  # + nape as the swept-back mass, and THE BUN (beat 1) as one big blob on
  # the crown's top-back — oversized, half the head's silhouette from
  # behind.
  # ============================================================
  blob head on skull at=0.50 offset=(0,0.030,-0.020) r=0.072 wide=1.00 tall=0.95 deep=0.95 blend=0.006 color=261b12 gloss=0.25
  blob head on skull at=0.55 offset=(0,0.100,-0.045) r=0.060 wide=1.00 tall=1.05 deep=1.00 blend=0.006 color=261b12 gloss=0.30
  # Swept fringe at the brow depth — the decal paints the hairline itself.
  blob head on skull at=0.50 offset=(0,0.058,0.038) r=0.045 wide=1.25 tall=0.90 deep=0.90 blend=0.004 color=261b12 gloss=0.25
  # Nape closing to the neck at the back.
  blob head on skull at=0.50 offset=(0,-0.055,-0.060) r=0.045 wide=0.85 tall=1.00 deep=1.00 blend=0.005 color=261b12 gloss=0.30
  # Chin: a definite small point.
  blob head on skull at=0.50 offset=(0,-0.105,0.060) r=0.018 wide=1.10 tall=0.60 deep=0.90 blend=0.004

  # ============================================================
  # ARMS — slim, pale upper arms BARE (the pale block that echoes the face),
  # black opera gloves from above the elbow to the fingertips. Slimmer than
  # the schoolgirl's: the reference's limbs are slender.
  # ============================================================
  blob arm on clavicle at=1.00 offset=(0,-0.016,0) r=0.029 tall=0.85 blend=0.005 mirror core
  bar  arm on upperarm from=0.05 to=0.98 r=0.026 r2=0.022 blend=0.005 mirror
  # The glove line: skin to just above the elbow, black below.
  blob arm on forearm  at=0.00 r=0.023 blend=0.005 mirror
  bar  arm on forearm  from=0.02 to=0.30 r=0.022 r2=0.021 blend=0.004 mirror
  bar  arm on forearm  from=0.30 to=0.98 r=0.021 r2=0.018 blend=0.004 mirror color=171219
  # Gloved hand — a slim smooth mitt, no fingers (house rule: only the
  # goblin's hand articulates).
  blob arm on hand at=0.50 offset=(0,0,0.020) r=0.023 wide=0.85 tall=1.10 deep=1.20 blend=0.004 mirror color=171219

  # ============================================================
  # LEGS — black stockings as paint below the skirt hem; slim (the
  # reference's calves carry no bulge). Thigh cross-section deeper than
  # wide, as measured on the schoolgirl.
  # ============================================================
  blob leg on thigh at=0.00 r=0.060 deep=1.08 blend=0.006 mirror core color=171219
  bar  leg on thigh from=0.02 to=1.00 r=0.064 r2=0.040 deep=1.08 blend=0.005 mirror color=171219
  blob leg on shin  at=0.00 r=0.040 deep=1.05 blend=0.005 mirror color=171219
  bar  leg on shin  from=0.02 to=1.00 r=0.042 r2=0.031 blend=0.005 mirror color=171219

  # ============================================================
  # SHOES — black heeled pumps (the schoolgirl's mary-jane pattern, ankle at
  # 0.115, same world-displacement authoring), glossier than the dress.
  # ============================================================
  blob leg on foot at=0.00 r=0.028 r2=0.024 wide=1.70 tall=1.05 deep=1.30 blend=0.006 offset=(0.002,-0.085,-0.050) tip=(0.010,-0.002,0.095) mirror color=171219 gloss=0.30
  blob leg on foot at=0.00 r=0.036 wide=1.15 tall=0.95 deep=1.25 blend=0.006 offset=(-0.004,-0.030,0.000) mirror color=171219 gloss=0.30

# ============================================================
# FACE BLOCK — a small oval skull under the hair: narrower jaw, light brow,
# a small nose. The face ITSELF is the baked decal below; three dispatches
# proved painted-prim features read as a visor band, so none are added.
# ============================================================
face
  headRadius 0.068
  headWidth  0.92
  headHeight 1.28
  headDepth  1.10
  jawWidth   0.78
  jawHeight  0.72
  jawDrop    0.058
  jawJut     0.036
  noseLength 0.036
  noseWidth  0.633
  noseDrop   0.022
  browHeavy  0.002
  browRise   0.022
  headBlend  0.005

# Her own face, baked flat off the reference mesh's head (npm run
# blob:face-bake -- female --head-frac 1.0, head meshes only — the clothes
# were filtered out first) and pasted on. `decal 1` is load-bearing: the
# loader fetches the baked PNG only if decal > 0.5.
#
# The bake frames bun-to-chin: eyes at bake v ~0.53, mouth v ~0.70. First
# projection is the schoolgirl's solve scaled to this skull, tuned by eye
# from the turntable frames — the frames win over arithmetic.
sheet
  image       female-face.png
  decal       0
  projScaleX  0.19
  projScaleY  0.23
  projCentreX 0.50
  projCentreY 0.45
  # Owner-tuned in the lab, 2026-09-05. eyeGlowAmp 0.25 against a 1.6 default
  # and eyeGlowCut 0.69 against 0.88: her glow is a COLD catchlight in a pale
  # face, not the soldier's burning red -- amp near the floor keeps it a
  # highlight rather than an emitter, and the low cut is what lets the bake's
  # own eye texels clear the mask at all.
  eyeGlowAmp  0.25
  eyeGlowCut  0.69
  texRelief   1.400
  texStrength 1.000

# PALE skin — the widow has not seen the sun. sRGB ~(232,205,190) -> linear.
# Dry, matte, almost no mottle: she is porcelain, not latex. Wounds stay
# red.
palette
  baseColor     0.80 0.62 0.52
  deepColor     0.50 0.08 0.08
  charColor     0.22 0.13 0.10
  specIntensity 0.40
  specRoughness 0.45
  fresnelBoost  0.28
  translucency  0.22
  wetness       0.10
  mottleAmp     0.03
  mottleScale   1.2
  mottleColor   0.55 0.38 0.28
